# Installed packages. The app itself ships no runtime dependencies; this is only
# ever the lint tooling, which is restored from package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# Local backups exported from the app
backups/
*.backup.json

# Working artifacts, held local by rule rather than by anyone remembering. `.copilot-tracking/`
# holds one directory per phase per session; six of those files, all from the first task, are
# committed and are the closest thing this repository has to a design rationale. Everything a later
# session writes there is working evidence for that session and stays on the machine that wrote it.
# `.github/prompts/` holds spent instructions to an agent, which BL-060 parked rather than commit.
#
# A rule rather than a list, because a list is a thing someone has to keep complete. Git ignores
# have no effect on a file that is already tracked, so the six committed artifacts are untouched
# while everything added later is held out by construction, and nobody has to maintain an
# exception for them. `npm run publication` checks that both rules are still in force, because an
# ignore rule that has been deleted looks exactly like one that was never needed.
.copilot-tracking/
.github/prompts/
